    "title": "pandas.IntervalIndex.closed — pandas 2.2.3 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.IntervalIndex.closed#\n\n- IntervalIndex.closed[source]#\n- String describing the inclusive side the intervals. Either `left` ,`right` ,`both` or`neither` .Examples For arrays: >>> interv_arr = pd.arrays.IntervalArray([pd.Interval(0, 1), pd.Interval(1, 5)]) >>> interv_arr <IntervalArray> [(0, 1], (1, 5]] Length: 2, dtype: interval[int64, right] >>> interv_arr.closed 'right' For Interval Index: >>> interv_idx = pd.interval_range(start=0, end=2) >>> interv_idx IntervalIndex([(0, 1], (1, 2]], dtype='interval[int64, right]') >>> interv_idx.closed 'right'",
